# AI Shelf flow definitions

When the user asks to create or edit an automation flow for AI Shelf, output a **`.flow.md`** file.

## File format

- YAML frontmatter + Markdown body (the body is the Claude agent prompt when `runner: claude`).
- Save under `%APPDATA%/ai-shelf/flows/{id}.flow.md` (or project `flows/` folder).

## Required frontmatter

```yaml
---
schema: ai-shelf.flow/definition/v1
id: my-flow-id
enabled: true
timeout_sec: 600
phases:
  - id: step-one
    label: Short human label
  - id: step-two
    label: Another step
---
```

## Optional frontmatter

```yaml
schedule: "0 9 * * 1-5"   # cron, Asia/Taipei unless timezone set (min 1h between fires)
timezone: Asia/Taipei
runner: claude            # default | http for simple checks
tool_args: --model haiku  # default for claude runner when omitted
orchestration: true       # force multi-node mode (also auto when phases set tool/kind/retry/gate)
extra_mcp_servers:        # optional — external MCP from Claude config
  - atlassian
```

## Multi-agent orchestration (per-phase nodes)

When any phase sets `tool`, `kind`, `retry`, `require_approval`, `next`, `on_fail`, or `on_reject` (or `orchestration: true`), the runner executes **one process per phase**:

```yaml
orchestration: true
phases:
  - id: research
    label: Research with Claude
    tool: claude
  - id: review
    label: Human review
    kind: gate
    on_reject: fail
  - id: draft
    label: Draft with Codex
    tool: codex
    retry: 1
    on_fail: skip
```

- Node output is written to `runs/{runId}/phases/{id}/output.md` and injected into the next phase prompt.
- `kind: gate` pauses for Approve / Reject in the UI.
- Supported tools: `claude`, `cursor` (or `agent`), `codex`, `gemini`.

Legacy flows without these fields still run as a **single agent** for the whole body.

## Claude runner protocol

The body must instruct the agent to report progress with MCP tools `flow_progress` and `flow_output` (spawned by the runner). Fallback: stdout `FLOW_PROGRESS` lines.

The runner also injects bundled **system skills** from `src/flow/system-skills/` into every agent run (e.g. mandatory `flow_output` on success and failure).

Mark each major step in the body with a heading that includes the phase id:

```markdown
## 【step-one】Gather data

...
```

End output after the line `FLOW_OUTPUT_BEGIN` (the runner captures everything after as `output.md`).

## HTTP runner

For connectivity or simple API checks without Claude:

```yaml
runner: http
url: https://www.google.com
method: HEAD
phases:
  - id: check
    label: HTTP check
```

## Examples

- Daily report: `schedule: "0 8 * * *"`, multiple phases, `on_fail: slack`
- Weekly cleanup: `schedule: "0 3 * * 0"`
- Manual only: omit `schedule`
- Multi-agent pipeline: per-phase `tool` + optional `kind: gate`

One markdown file = one DAG defined by `phases` order (and optional `next` / `on_fail` branches).
